# 36_shamanic_trance_drum.ledc — Shamanic Trance (Monaural Drum), ~30 min
# ALTERED STATE: the "shamanic state of consciousness" — a deep theta drum-trance for inner
#   journeying, driven by a monotonous ~4.5 Hz drum. Scaffolding for the practice, not a guarantee
#   of any state. Arc: settle ~8 Hz -> descend to 4.5 Hz journey drum (16 min hold) -> faster
#   "callback" 4.5->9 Hz -> gentle wake to ~10 Hz.
#
# V2 FEATURES USED (and why):
#   * MONAURAL beat (two pan=0 channels at 160 and 160+beat) — the drum forms ACOUSTICALLY in the
#     air (~50 dB modulation, vs binaural's ~3 dB), so it works on a single speaker or one ear: the
#     stronger, more robust driver, ideal for a hands-free journeying drum (playbook A1,
#     guidelines §4 monaural). The beat glides by ramping the SECOND channel's carrier (freq IS
#     interpolatable), 160/168 (8 Hz) -> 160/164.5 (4.5 Hz).
#   * LED env=3 (TRAPEZOID gate) + attack — the amber light "drum flash" uses a crisp trapezoid
#     luminance gate with a soft 6 ms raised edge, matching the percussive character of the drum
#     (playbook A2/B2) rather than a smooth sine.
#   * Audio env=3 trapezoid + duty + attack — a low 137 Hz isochronic "hit" (35% duty, 8 ms edge)
#     reinforces the drum with a felt pulse.
#   * Audio JITTER (0.3 Hz over 53 s) on the isochronic drum's pulse rate — a slow non-repeating
#     wander that keeps a 16-minute monotonous drum from habituating, sustaining the trance
#     (playbook A3). On a non-binaural channel jitter wanders the mod (pulse) rate.
#   * BROWN-noise AM bed with ROTATING PAN (~-100:100 over 8 s) — a warm, gated brown-noise
#     underlayer that slowly circles the head for immersion (playbook A6/A8).
#
# RESEARCH / PATENT CITATION:
#   ~4-4.5 Hz theta drumming -> shamanic trance: Maxfield's finding that a steady ~4.5 Hz drum held
#   >=15 min reliably shifts practitioners into theta trance (see 19_shamanic_journey and
#   entrainment_techniques_playbook.md §C). Monaural beats A1, trapezoid iso A2, AM-noise A6,
#   rotating pan A8. Core techniques are expired prior art (Nagle US 4,191,175 pulsed-noise;
#   patent_landscape_ave.md).
#
# SAFETY / CONTRAINDICATIONS:
#   Do NOT use if you have photosensitive epilepsy, a seizure disorder, or a history of photic
#   migraine. Do not use while driving or operating machinery. Stop if you feel dizzy or unwell.
#   EXPERIENTIAL, not medical. Every rate is <=10 Hz (below the 15-25 Hz photosensitive band); warm
#   amber is NOT saturated red (R/(R+G+B)=220/330=0.67<0.8); no red<->blue; brightness dim (<=26%)
#   with a floor; the 8 ms trapezoid attack keeps every flash/pulse click-free; light ramps in 20 s
#   and fades out over the wake, never stopped abruptly. Eyes closed, lying down. Engine note: AM
#   depth is fixed (~0.1) here, so the trapezoid pulse is a gentle buzz, not a hard on/off.
#
# Duration: ~30 min.  LED cols: time freq duty bright R G B mask env phase attack
#   Audio: A time freq pan vol mod [ch] [freqR] [wave] [duty] [env] [phase] [attack] [jitter]
#   (env 3 = trapezoid gate; wave 6 = brown noise).
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (the > prefix sits where a segment BEGINS).

# --- Brown-noise bed (runs throughout, fades in first) ---
A 0 90 ~-100:100:8000 >0 4.5 4 0 6 50 1       # ch4 BROWN bed: 4.5 Hz sine-gated, rotating pan (8 s cycle); vol fade-in
A 60000 90 ~-100:100:8000 25 4.5 4 0 6 50 1   # ch4 brown settled 25 (warm underlayer)

# --- Settle / drum 8 Hz (00:00-03:00): warm amber trapezoid flash + drum fade in ---
0 8 50 >0 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # amber 8 Hz TRAPEZOID flash (env 3, 6 ms edge); bright fade-in
A 0 160 0 >0 0 1 0 0                          # ch1 monaural carrier A (160 Hz, pan 0); vol fade-in
A 0 168 0 >0 0 2 0 0                          # ch2 monaural carrier B (168 Hz, pan 0) => 8 Hz drum in the air
A 0 137 0 >0 8 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000       # ch3 iso drum hit: 137 Hz, 8 Hz trapezoid gate, 35% duty, 8 ms edge; pulse jitter 0.3 Hz/53 s
S 5000 default 10 "Lie down and let the drum find its rhythm around you. Let it carry you toward the journey."
20000 8 50 26 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # brightness reaches 26% (>=15 s ramp-in)
A 45000 160 0 50 0 1 0 0                      # ch1 vol settled 50
A 45000 168 0 50 0 2 0 0                      # ch2 vol settled 50 (drum steady 8 Hz)
A 45000 137 0 40 8 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000   # ch3 iso drum settled 40
45000 8 50 ~14:30:12000 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # breathing brightness LFO engages (0.1 Hz)

# --- Descent (03:00-08:00): drum 8 -> 4.5 Hz (~0.7 Hz/min) ---
A 180000 160 0 50 0 1 0 0                     # ch1 carrier A held at 160 (the anchor tone)
A 180000 >168 0 50 0 2 0 0                    # ch2 carrier B ramps 168->164.5 => monaural beat 8->4.5
A 180000 137 0 40 >8 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000 # ch3 iso pulse ramps 8->4.5 (mod IS interpolatable); jitter on
180000 >8 50 ~14:30:12000 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # LED flash tracks the drum 8->4.5, breathing continues
S 180000 default 10 "Let the drum slow and carry you downward, into the between-place."

# --- Journey hold (08:00-24:00 = 16 min): the monotonous 4.5 Hz drum, jitter sustains it ---
A 480000 164.5 0 55 0 2 0 0                   # ch2 carrier B at 164.5 => 4.5 Hz monaural drum, fuller vol
A 480000 137 0 45 4.5 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000 # ch3 iso drum at 4.5 Hz, jitter drifting the pulse
480000 4.5 50 ~14:30:12000 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # amber 4.5 Hz trapezoid flash 1:1, gentle breathing LFO
S 480000 default 10 "You are in the journey now. Let the steady drum hold you. Travel, and let it be your thread home."
S 1080000 default 10 "Wander freely. The drum will not let you lose your way; it beats on beneath everything."

# --- Callback (24:00-27:00): the drummer's faster recall, drum 4.5 -> 9 Hz ---
A 1440000 >164.5 0 55 0 2 0 0                 # ch2 carrier B ramps 164.5->169 => monaural beat 4.5->9 (the recall)
A 1440000 137 0 45 >4.5 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000 # ch3 iso pulse 4.5->9 lockstep
1440000 >4.5 50 26 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # LED 4.5->9; steady 26% for the alerting callback (LFO dropped)
S 1440000 default 10 "The drum is calling you back. Begin to return, following the quickening beat homeward."

# --- Gentle wake (27:00-30:00): drum 9 -> 10 Hz + soft fade ---
A 1620000 160 0 >50 0 1 0 0                   # ch1 carrier A vol fades 50->0
A 1620000 >169 0 >55 0 2 0 0                  # ch2 carrier B 169->170 (beat 9->10) and vol fades 55->0
A 1620000 137 0 >45 >9 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000 # ch3 iso pulse 9->10, vol fades 45->0
A 1620000 90 ~-100:100:8000 >25 4.5 4 0 6 50 1  # brown bed fades 25->0
1620000 >9 50 >26 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # LED 9->10, brightness fades 26->0
S 1620000 default 10 "Come fully back to the room now. Feel the ground beneath you, and open your eyes when you are ready."
A 1800000 160 0 0 0 1 0 0                      # end: ch1 vol 0
A 1800000 170 0 0 0 2 0 0                      # end: ch2 vol 0 (beat settled 10)
A 1800000 137 0 0 10 3 0 0 35 3 0 8 0.3:53000  # end: ch3 vol 0
A 1800000 90 ~-100:100:8000 0 4.5 4 0 6 50 1   # end: brown bed 0
1800000 10 50 0 220 110 0 15 3 0 6   # end: brightness 0

S 1800000 default 20 "WAKE UP!"
S 1810000 default 40 "WAKE UP!"
S 1820000 default 50 "WAKE UP!"
S 1830000 default 60 "WAKE UP!"
